  "difficulty_level": "H3",
  "difficulty_reason": "The theorem extends a prescribed finite-type integer model of a quasi-compact open across an arbitrary qcqs scheme. Its proof builds fibre-product rings, recovers standard affine opens after finite-stage descent, manufactures finite-type subalgebra models, and synchronizes two-level directed gluing with affine transitions. This global relative Noetherian approximation construction is substantially beyond ordinary affine finite-presentation descent.",
